				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/huitzil" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(375435); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=375435&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606207903" alt="Huitzil" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=375435)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/huitzil" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(375435); return false;" >Huitzil</a></span> <span class="odate time_1401178051 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 May 2014 08:07</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2039859">
									

<p>This has a nice tone and feel to it but it has two of my biggest problems with SCPs:</p>
<p>First, it relies on handwaving something done by the foundation that would take preposterous amounts of manpower and resources, would be ridiculously unethical, and also still wouldn't work. In this case, brainwashing every single person who has ever heard of the moons of Jupiter to forget the existence of one of them, and then erasing records of it in every single written account going back to the 1600s, three separate times in the span of 20 years. No. That isn't happening, no organization could possibly have that level of resources, and the number of people who would be required to cooperate would not cooperate. The cover-up you describe is utterly impossible on any world that resembles our own, without employing plot devices that make all drama and humanity meaningless.</p>
<p>Second, it's gonna getcha. It's of unfathomable scale, it's from space, we don't know where it came from or why, but like <strong>every</strong> other thing we don't understand, it is *gonna getcha*. It's hard to buy that we're insignificant in the cosmos when one third of all objects in space were built for the purpose of killing us, and us specifically &#8212; we have to be REALLY important to be worth all that effort. It's hard to buy that &quot;we were just lucky&quot; to not be hit by this when placed next to the hundreds upon hundreds of objects that &quot;we were just lucky&quot; to not get getcha'd by. Hell, looking at how important we are, and how many things are aimed at us, and how something coincidentally stops all of them from killing us, the best conclusion to draw is that YHWH or someone an awful like Him actually exists and He's got our backs. Probably not the implication you want to give in horror fiction.</p>
<p>I would cut everything about it eating moons and the Foundation covering it up. That's completely unbelievable and eye-rolling. Jupiter has a dickton of minor moons &#8212; it's been eating those. We still don't know if we've mapped them all, so the Foundation could let the disappearance of minor moons look like &quot;well there's a lot we don't know about, there's a few of them that went back to areas we can't see.&quot; But as our technology gets better, people will be able to see that the moons are vanishing, and the Foundation doesn't know how to deal with that.</p>
<p>Second, I'd take out any reference to it being out to get us. No targeting the third planet. Third planet isn't important, has never been important. It's getting orders, we have observed the orders correspond to changes in its behavior, but maybe we cannot decipher them. We're afraid what they might be, so we made the BARRIER array; but it wasn't by unanimous verdict &#8212; some of the scientists and O5s think that whatever it does if cut off from command signals might be more dangerous to us than carrying out its orders; for all we know its orders are &quot;return to home base&quot; and its program when cut off from orders is to assume it is under attack and neutralize the source of jamming.</p>
<p>Also, how is it getting relevant command from 3 million light years away? Those are 3 million years old; even if it did crash more than 6 million years ago and transmit, why bother sending orders that will be responses 6 million years out of date? Furthermore, why have it RELY on up-to-the-minute commands that are six million years out of date &#8212; why wouldn't its actions be preprogrammed? You can go for a big time-scale, but 3 million LY is totally out of line. 175 LY or thereabouts is still unimaginably vast to a human mind, but it makes it such that Central Space Control is just now responding to what was happening around the time Cassini first spotted it. That creates a nice little parallel. It still doesn't quite solve the problem of it relying on constant new orders that are hundreds of years out of date, maybe that whole angle just has to be scrapped.</p>
<p>MAYBE, it was transmitting sensor data back to its home planet, which was only broadcasting back periodic messages just to aid in targeting where to send the sensor data too, and we figured out that it couldn't see Earth yet &#8212; but it would, as it had started fixing its sensors and a planetary alignment was approaching. So we put the array in place, not to keep it from being told to kill us, but to keep it from broadcasting our existence to its home. Only, we're not a hundred percent sure if the aliens would care we were there &#8212; and if they might send something to go check on a probe that stopped communicating.</p>

							</div>

								
					
