			<div class="content" id="post-content-2039968">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Due to application of amnestics, and an ongoing misinformation campaign, current information maintains that Jupiter has only ever had 4 moons. This program will remain in effect indefinitely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is breaking all credibility I could be building up to it. Just one of these is far too much. Amnestics erase memories, they don't erase the fact that anyone who looks at the Jovian system is going to see its moons with commercially available courtyard telescopes. We can't hope to take them <em>all</em> down, the amount of personnel required would be absurdly huge. It's an Ennui-5 Protocol in all its glory, being implemented every time a moon goes missing. It's too big. : /</p>
<p>Otherwise, I don't dislike it. Space things are nice, and this one has a potential (and accidental) connection with an article I'm currently rewriting for the main list, so&#8230; okay. Neutral vote for now. May come back to read it again.</p>
<p>Edit: Also, the entire BARRIER, Gigas and LEGIONNAIRE programs are simply excessive. This SCP is probably staged in the not-so-far future, 'cause even if every government in the planet bankrupts itself over and over again, we wouldn't be able to send a mass of projectiles such as Gigas or LEGIONNAIRE require. BARRIER&#8230; well, I'm not certain of how many satellites BARRIER implies, but I'm thinking less than a hundred. In any case, it's too many, I think. Dunno. Keeping the Neutral.</p>

							</div>

								
